{{Short description|Football competition}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=May 2018}}
The final tournament of the [[1938 FIFA World Cup]] was a [[single-elimination tournament]] involving the 16 teams which qualified for [[1938 FIFA World Cup|the tournament]]. The tournament began with the round of 16 on 4 June and concluded with the [[1938 FIFA World Cup final|final]] on 19 June 1938. [[Italy national football team|Italy]] won the final 4–2 for their second World Cup title.<ref>{{cite news |last=Molinaro |first=John F. |url=http://www.cbc.ca/sports/soccer/1938-world-cup-italy-repeats-as-champions-1.853724 |title=1938 World Cup: Italy repeats as champions |website=[[CBC Sports]] |publisher=[[Canadian Broadcasting Corporation]] |date=24 November 2009 |access-date=8 April 2018}}</ref>

Kick off times were scheduled at 17:00 for weekend matches (round of 16, quarter-finals and both finals), at 18:00 for matches in the middle of the week (semi-finals and replays).<ref>{{cite web |url=https://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k46351370/f2.item|work=[[L'Auto]]|date=4 June 1938|title=Le tournoi final de la troisième Coupe du Monde|language=fr| location=Paris, France|via=Gallica|page=2}}</ref>

