===Hungary vs Switzerland===
Hungary looked like the stronger team as the Swiss were missing key players such as [[Georges Aeby]] and [[Severino Minelli]]. Hungary took the lead with a header from [[György Sárosi]]. The result was in doubt for most of the second half, until [[Gyula Zsengellér]] sealed the game with a long-range effort in the dying minutes. Switzerland's manager [[Karl Rappan]] resigned after the game.<ref name="fiedler" />

