===Italy vs Brazil===
{{see also|Brazil–Italy football rivalry}}
The narrative leading to this highly anticipated match was built around an overconfident Brazil, who had impressed in the previous three matches. However, Italy had a better start to the game, creating the best chances but finding a well-positioned [[Walter (footballer, born 1912)|Walter]] stopping their attacks. In the second half, Italy soon found the net with [[Gino Colaussi|Colaussi]], before being awarded a penalty following a foul in the box by [[Domingos da Guia]], his third in the tournament. The penalty was calmly converted by [[Giuseppe Meazza|Meazza]]. At 2–0, Brazil pushed forward to break the Italian defence, but only managed to score a goal in the 87th minute with [[Romeu Pellicciari|Romeu]] scoring from a corner kick. Some tense moments followed, but Italy managed to hold out for the remaining time, reaching their second final in a row.<ref name="fiedler" />

